227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/ActualText (Unfortunately, it is often the case that when we talk about billions and trillions the numbers become abstract and potentially meaningless. This in itself is a major issue since the challenge we are facing with biodiversity is so large that it is hard for us as individuals to grasp the scale of its consequences. It is easier for us to be concerned about the pollution of a small nearby lake than the destruction of an ocean. Having said that, in nature, nothing is too small or too big, everything is interconnected. This inability to appreciate the impact of environmental degradation is made worse by our growing alienation from nature and the outdoors, or what author Richard Louv dubs Nature-Deficit Disorder .)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
