252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 152 0 R
/T (The Biodiversity Consultancy proposes a four-step biodiversity mitigation hierarchy : avoidance \(preventing impacts altogether\), minimization \(reducing harm\), restoration \(rehabilitating affected ecosystems\), and finally offsetting \(compensating for residual damage elsewhere and creating net positive impact\). The goal of this hierarchy is to guide decision-makers and developers toward a more sustainable approach to development, where efforts are made to conserve biodiversity and minimize environmental harm. )
/E (The Biodiversity Consultancy proposes a four-step biodiversity mitigation hierarchy : avoidance \(preventing impacts altogether\), minimization \(reducing harm\), restoration \(rehabilitating affected ecosystems\), and finally offsetting \(compensating for residual damage elsewhere and creating net positive impact\). The goal of this hierarchy is to guide decision-makers and developers toward a more sustainable approach to development, where efforts are made to conserve biodiversity and minimize environmental harm. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
