285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/ActualText (As highlighted earlier, biodiversity loss represents a significant social and economic risk for the world, and thus at a minimum and purely from a risk management standpoint, investors have a responsibility to account for and mitigate this risk. Nonetheless, unlike climate risk, tools to identify and manage biodiversity risks at the corporate level remain in their infancy.   )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/ActualText (In 2020, the UN PRI underlined a need for investors to act on biodiversity loss and called for investors to address this issue systematically rather than focus on individual holdings . The accompanying report made eight distinct investor-related biodiversity loss recommendations:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/ActualText (21)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/ActualText (Allocate capital to sectors or business models which are avoiding and reducing biodiversity loss and increase opportunities for positive outcomes on the ground, including restoration. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/ActualText (Engage investees on reducing negative biodiversity outcomes and design stewardship approaches to deliver positive biodiversity outcomes.)
